LICENCE - nonfree/aic8800d80

READ THIS FIRST. Unlike nonfree/brcm43455, these files arrive WITHOUT a licence from the company that
wrote them. AICSemi (Beijing Aicxin Semiconductor) has published no terms for this firmware that this
project could find. This file says what IS known, and does not pretend to more. docs/licensing.md
section 5a records the decision to carry them anyway, and why it is an exception.

What is known, and from where:

1. The files were taken from Radxa's packaging repository, https://github.com/radxa-pkg/aic8800, at
   commit 09c65d618f5ccde3233f8f41ef2f55b205ef11db ("feat: update to
   aic8800d_linux_sdk_V4.0_2025_0410_b99ca8b6"), path src/SDIO/driver_fw/fw/aic8800D80/. That
   repository's debian/copyright, at the same commit, has a single stanza covering every file in it,
   firmware included. It is reproduced here verbatim:

     Format: https://www.debian.org/doc/packaging-manuals/copyright-format/1.0/
     Upstream-Name: aic8800
     Source: https://github.com/radxa-pkg/aic8800

     Files: *
     Copyright: © 2025 Radxa Computer Co., Ltd
     License: GPL-3+

     License: GPL-3+
      This program is free software; you can redistribute it and/or modify
      it under the terms of the GNU General Public License as published by
      the Free Software Foundation; either version 3, or (at your option)
      any later version.
      .
      This program is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but
      WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied warranty of
      MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.  See the GNU
      General Public License for more details.
      .
      You should have received a copy of the GNU General Public License
      along with this program; if not, write to the Free Software
      Foundation, Inc., 51 Franklin St, Fifth Floor, Boston, MA
      02110-1301, USA.
      .
      On Debian systems, the complete text of the GNU General Public License
      can be found in /usr/share/common-licenses/GPL-3.

   This project does NOT read that stanza as AICSemi granting anything. A GPL grant on a binary with no
   source offered is not a coherent licence, and Radxa is not the author of this firmware. It is
   recorded because it is the only written term these files travel under, and the terms must travel
   with every copy.

2. Gentoo packages the same firmware (net-wireless/aic8800) under the licence label "freedist" -
   freely redistributable. That is a distribution's classification, not a text from the vendor.

3. StarFive ships these exact files, byte for byte, in the official Debian image for the VisionFive 2
   Lite, the board this project drives them on. The board's own boot log recorded an MD5 for each file
   as its driver loaded it, and all five match the copies here (see PROVENANCE).

What GodspeedOS does with them: uploads them, unmodified, to the AIC8800D80's own processor over SDIO,
and speaks to the firmware through the protocol it exposes. It does not modify, decompile or
disassemble them.

If AICSemi, StarFive or Radxa publish terms for this firmware, they replace this file, and if those terms
forbid redistribution the files leave this repository for scripts/get_firmware.py.
